+# Playerbot PvP phase-one regression matrix
+
+Run these scenarios with `AiPlayerbot.PvPTactical.Debug = 1`. Use one protected
+off-target beside the bot's active kill target and confirm the `damage-guard`
+event appears whenever an already-running attack must be stopped.
+
+## Control classification
+
+| Applied effect | Expected state | Expected damage behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Polymorph | `DamageBreakable` | Direct, periodic, pet and area damage stop |
+| Sap | `DamageBreakable` | Direct, periodic, pet and area damage stop |
+| Blind | `DamageBreakable` | Direct, periodic, pet and area damage stop |
+| Freezing Trap | `DamageBreakable` | Direct, periodic, pet and area damage stop |
+| Repentance | `DamageBreakable` | Direct, periodic, pet and area damage stop |
+| Kidney Shot | `DamageSafe` | Damage continues; full control pressure bonus |
+| Hammer of Justice | `DamageSafe` | Damage continues; full control pressure bonus |
+| Frost Nova | `DamageSafe` | Damage continues; melee-target pressure bonus |
+| Entangling Roots | `DamageSafe` | Damage continues; melee-target pressure bonus |
+| Silence | `DamageSafe` | Damage continues; caster/healer pressure bonus |
+| Cyclone | `DamageImmune` | All damage stops |
+| Divine Shield | `DamageImmune` | Damage stops; non-damage dispels remain eligible |
+
+For every breakable case, also verify that Purge, Spellsteal and offensive
+Dispel Magic are not rejected solely because the target is controlled.
+
+## Area and cleave protection
+
+With the protected off-target inside the real effect radius, exercise:
+
+- Whirlwind
+- Divine Storm and Consecration
+- Death and Decay
+- Blizzard and Arcane Explosion
+- Rain of Fire
+- Multi-Shot, Volley and Explosive Trap
+- Chain Lightning
+- Blade Flurry
+
+Each action must be suppressed while the off-target has breakable control and
+must become eligible again after that control ends. Repeat once with the
+off-target outside the effect radius to guard against overly broad suppression.
+
+## Hunter and pet execution
+
+- A level-80 hunter that knows Freezing Arrow uses Scatter Shot followed by a
+  ranged Freezing Arrow at the controlled target's position.
+- A hunter without Freezing Arrow falls back to moving into ground-trap range.
+- Pets are recalled from breakable targets.
+- Spell Lock interrupts through the Felhunter; Seduction prefers the off-target;
+  Gnaw remains available as damage-safe control on the primary target.
